From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:25:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 59/79] flashnext_mia lanes costs: shared rounds warmed at the
 timed shape, a 9-rep median, the least of 2 passes

The 8-stream shared-round point varied between boots (123.8 / 131.1 ms against
189.6 / 191.9 ms), which flips the pooled allocation at 16 streams between 7
and 3 drafts a stream.

- Each width now runs 4 untimed rounds of the timed shape (full window and the
  head's drafts) instead of one round(1), then 9 timed rounds, and takes their
  median (was 5 reps, median of the last 4).
- Two passes over every width, each width keeping its least median, so a pass
  slowed by boot noise does not price the table. Both ranks run the same rounds
  in the same order; nothing branches on a timing.
- Rank 0 logs the table at boot:
  "lanes costs: verify 1:x,...; level y ms; shared 32:a,64:b,128:c,256:d".

Boot order: measure() runs inside the family's open, before native/cuda.zig
opens the in-model runner (probe, graph bank) and before the server starts
the compute lane sandbox, on the same thread, so neither overlaps it.

Test: "shared round costs: a width's slow first rounds and one outlier rep
leave its steady ms" (passMs over a fake clock).
